From 6bbed30dcf1b9e14c75c67773602391c329c28cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zixuan Zhang <zixuan.zhang.uj@renesas.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:57:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: adv7511: accept the pinned mode without its
 aspect ratio

With "renesas,seamless-boot-logo-vic" set, adv7511_bridge_mode_valid()
rejects every mode that is not drm_mode_equal() to the CEA mode the
connector is pinned to.  drm_mode_equal() also compares the picture
aspect ratio, and that breaks every plain DRM/KMS client:

  - the CEA table gives VIC 16 a 16:9 aspect ratio;
  - a client that has not set DRM_CLIENT_CAP_ASPECT_RATIO receives the
    mode from GETCONNECTOR with the DRM_MODE_FLAG_PIC_AR_* bits cleared;
  - handing it back through SETCRTC, drm_mode_convert_umode() turns the
    missing bits into HDMI_PICTURE_ASPECT_NONE;
  - drm_atomic_helper_check_modeset() calls the bridge's mode_valid,
    the modes no longer compare equal, and the modeset fails with
    -EINVAL ("[BRIDGE] mode_valid() failed").

Weston sets the capability, which is why this went unnoticed; a boot
logo application written against libdrm in the usual way - or modetest -
does not, and never gets a picture up.  Seen on the RZ/G3L EVK.

The aspect ratio is metadata for the AVI InfoFrame, not something the
hardware scans out.  Compare timings, clock, flags and 3D flags, which
is everything the pinning is there to protect.  Aspect-ratio-aware
clients still receive the mode as 16:9 from get_modes().

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [RZ/G3L boot logo, board specific]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7511_drv.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7511_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7511_drv.c
index 76f24b2..216febc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7511_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7511_drv.c
@@ -1043,7 +1043,20 @@ static enum drm_mode_status adv7511_bridge_mode_valid(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 		if (!pinned)
 			return MODE_ERROR;
 
-		match = drm_mode_equal(pinned, mode);
+		/*
+		 * Compare what the hardware scans out - timings, clock and
+		 * flags - and not the picture aspect ratio.  The CEA mode
+		 * carries 16:9, but a client that has not asked for
+		 * DRM_CLIENT_CAP_ASPECT_RATIO gets the mode with the aspect
+		 * ratio stripped and hands it back as "none".  With
+		 * drm_mode_equal() that is a different mode, and every plain
+		 * DRM/KMS program's first modeset fails with -EINVAL.
+		 */
+		match = drm_mode_match(pinned, mode,
+				       DRM_MODE_MATCH_TIMINGS |
+				       DRM_MODE_MATCH_CLOCK |
+				       DRM_MODE_MATCH_FLAGS |
+				       DRM_MODE_MATCH_3D_FLAGS);
 		drm_mode_destroy(bridge->dev, pinned);
 
 		if (!match)
